cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or parts of its code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NDM File Timestamp"
abstract: >-
  A single Bash script that proves a file existed, unchanged, at a given time: several
  independent Time Stamping Authorities sign its SHA-256 hash with RFC 3161 timestamps,
  and the proofs can be verified at any time, even after the TSA certificates expire.
  The file, its proofs, the trusted root certificates and the script can be packed into
  one self-contained archive that verifies offline.
authors:
